(7738170, 1275744, 114285, '<td valign="top">Oh man, so sorry to hear, I guess you persisted ;)<br/> <br/>How did the gear turn out?</td>', 'Oh man, so sorry to hear, I guess you persisted ;) How did the gear turn out?', '2023-02-08 19:29:06.000000', NULL, 0),
(7738180, 1275744, 29535, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by Neat:</b></div><hr/><i> Oh man, so sorry to hear, I guess you persisted ;)<br/> <br/>How did the gear turn out? </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Ha! The irony was not lost when this started to do relatively well...<br/> <br/>The gear really impressed me to be fair. Everything was in my Manfrotto backpack which is water repellant - not waterproof - but did the job nicely. The tripod has a few battle scars on the head from where it bounced off a rock but it''s otherwise perfect despite being underwater for ten minutes or so while I got my main kit to a safe space.<br/> <br/>Just my pride was hurt :D now I know to bring wellies and not try to use a tripod as a walking stick at least.</td>', 'Originally posted by Neat: Oh man, so sorry to hear, I guess you persisted ;) How did the gear turn out?   Ha! The irony was not lost when this started to do relatively well... The gear really impressed me to be fair. Everything was in my Manfrotto backpack which is water repellant - not waterproof - but did the job nicely. The tripod has a few battle scars on the head from where it bounced off a rock but it''s otherwise perfect despite being underwater for ten minutes or so while I got my main kit to a safe space. Just my pride was hurt :D now I know to bring wellies and not try to use a tripod as a walking stick at least.', '2023-02-09 02:35:34.000000', NULL, 0),
